The mosaic is 3 inches tall.
Let $x$ be the length of the mosaic in inches.
The area of the mosaic is $3x$ square inches.
The number of chips needed is $12 \times 3x = 36x$.
Since Milo has 144 chips, we have $36x = 144$.
Dividing both sides by 36, we get $x = \frac{144}{36} = 4$.
Therefore, he can make the mosaic 4 inches long.

